346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Traders cannot use the credit from selling T1 holdings BTST on the same day due to regulatory requirements. When you sell T1 holdings, the EPI process cannot begin until your shares settle in your demat account. Therefore, traders can only use proceeds from selling T1 holdings from the next trading day when the shares are settled. The credit from selling T1 holdings \(BTST trades\) cannot be used on the same day as per regulations \(PDF\). This means traders cannot use the proceeds from your BTST sale immediately.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (This creates severe capital inefficiency for active traders. They may miss on opportunities to capitalize on intraday movements, cannot rotate capital quickly across different stocks, and effectively have reduced buying power despite having completed your sale. It becomes a major issue for traders with limited capital as well.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
