444 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 148 0 R
/T (On 5th December 2025, Internet Security Giant Cloudflare went down due to multiple simultaneous issues faced by the company, the most notable one being a zero-day React.js vulnerability \(CVE-2025-55182\).  Since Cloudflare was the DDoS protection provider and Reverse Proxy provider for major brokers, including Zerodha, Groww, and Angel One, their services were severely impacted during the outage. This lasted for around 1 hour during a high-intensity RBI Policy announcement.  During this, users faced login failures, order execution & cancellation errors, and web portal inaccessibility during a critical market period. This incident is of profound importance to us because it reveals something important and disturbing about the system. It showed us that multiple major brokerage platforms could get impacted at once, without the need for any foul play. Such events could occur during heightened market activity linked to a major macro announcement. how external infrastructure dependencies can cause systemic broker downtime, even when exchange core systems are functioning.   )
/E (On 5th December 2025, Internet Security Giant Cloudflare went down due to multiple simultaneous issues faced by the company, the most notable one being a zero-day React.js vulnerability \(CVE-2025-55182\).  Since Cloudflare was the DDoS protection provider and Reverse Proxy provider for major brokers, including Zerodha, Groww, and Angel One, their services were severely impacted during the outage. This lasted for around 1 hour during a high-intensity RBI Policy announcement.  During this, users faced login failures, order execution & cancellation errors, and web portal inaccessibility during a critical market period. This incident is of profound importance to us because it reveals something important and disturbing about the system. It showed us that multiple major brokerage platforms could get impacted at once, without the need for any foul play. Such events could occur during heightened market activity linked to a major macro announcement. how external infrastructure dependencies can cause systemic broker downtime, even when exchange core systems are functioning.   )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
