/T (- The "Zero Brokerage" model, which gained prominence by offering free equity delivery trading, is driving a massive, irreversible shift toward transparency in the financial services industry, particularly in India.  - As of 2026, while it has democratized access to the stock market, the model faces significant sustainability challenges due to regulatory curbs, high client acquisition costs, and reliance on alternative revenue streams like derivatives trading.  - By 2030, the industry is expected to evolve into a hybrid, technology-driven ecosystem where "zero" becomes the baseline for service, but not necessarily "zero cost" to the user.)
/E (- The "Zero Brokerage" model, which gained prominence by offering free equity delivery trading, is driving a massive, irreversible shift toward transparency in the financial services industry, particularly in India.  - As of 2026, while it has democratized access to the stock market, the model faces significant sustainability challenges due to regulatory curbs, high client acquisition costs, and reliance on alternative revenue streams like derivatives trading.  - By 2030, the industry is expected to evolve into a hybrid, technology-driven ecosystem where "zero" becomes the baseline for service, but not necessarily "zero cost" to the user.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [15]
