/E (Inference The survey indicates that the main factors encouraging respondents to invest more in equities are low returns on traditional assets and easy access through trading apps, each influencing 47.1% of respondents. Additionally, 26.5% reported that advice from peers or media and increased income/savings motivated their investments. This suggests that both digital accessibility and dissatisfaction with traditional investment returns are key drivers behind the growing interest in equity markets among young investors.)
