/T (Inference From the 34 responses, the biggest factor that would reduce frustration is better learning support \(35.3%\), followed closely by lower costs \(32.4%\). Fewer respondents prioritized a more stable platform \(17.6%\) and better UI \(11.8%\), while emotional and mental support tools received the least interest \(~3%\). Users mainly want stronger learning support and lower costs to reduce frustration.)
/E (Inference From the 34 responses, the biggest factor that would reduce frustration is better learning support \(35.3%\), followed closely by lower costs \(32.4%\). Fewer respondents prioritized a more stable platform \(17.6%\) and better UI \(11.8%\), while emotional and mental support tools received the least interest \(~3%\). Users mainly want stronger learning support and lower costs to reduce frustration.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [10]
